                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><em>Trends in Anesthesiology</em> is a general education elective course designed for undergraduate medical students. It provides a systematic overview of recent advances in the theories, technologies, and clinical practice of modern anesthesiology. The course focuses on emerging topics such as enhanced recovery after surgery (ERAS), perioperative assessment and optimization, the effects of anesthesia on oncologic surgical and cognitive outcomes, airway management, and pain management. Through the integration of simulation-based teaching, the course strengthens students’ abilities in crisis management and team collaboration. The overarching aim is to deepen students’ understanding of anesthesiology and perioperative medicine, while fostering a humanistic medical perspective that emphasizes respect for life and the assurance of patient safety and comfort.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
